<title>INDIA: INDIAN SOYBEAN STEADY, OIL DOWN, MEAL EASY.</title>
<headline>INDIAN SOYBEAN STEADY, OIL DOWN, MEAL EASY.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets in very thin trading on Wednesday, dealers said. Business was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>All the major central Indian markets were closed in response to a strike call by the Hindu nationalist Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) to protest the murder of a party lawmaker in the central Indian city of Indore.</p>
<p>Soyoil refined was down by 100 rupees per tonne on poor demand against increased supplies, while soyoil solvent was steady. Business volume was steady and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained easy on poor export demand. Soymeal yellow was $261-262 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) to west Indian ports. Rapeseed extraction was $93 to $94 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export and was 3,150 to 3,200 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
